[block'ORD-0027-ast-space'
  [ctx'the spec of EMS-002','.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml']
  [ctx'the map of the inclusion','.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-INCLUSION.md']
  [tgt'the way back through fromAST writes the space a name needs from the prose after it, so a known command never turns unknown on the way back, by the inclusion the Regent decided on 2026-10-25; an ORD of the batch the version moves once for']
  [ctx'measured at d739544, section 3 of the intake: fromAST writes a text child glued to the name of the command that holds it, so a context command holding the prose foo comes back as the unknown command ctxfoo; and a mood header before prose reads the first word of the prose as one more mood code']
  [cnst'two pieces written side by side read as one when a name ends the first and a name starts the second, or the first ends a mood header; a space between them is what the source had, and whitespace between tokens is no node, so it costs nothing on the way in']
  [cnst'no oracle entry exercises it, so the suite gains a test whose fromAST calls the oracle records, and the Rust is ported byte for byte']
  [val'the space','the sources the test names come back to the same XML through fromAST; seen failing before it counts, and the Rust answers byte for byte']
